00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:39.180
I mean, I agree to some extent.

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:46.260
I think a lot of it is, okay, so you get, like, some iframes when you're turning around.

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:49.540
Like, you can also do, like, a spinorama.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:53.200
And I'm pretty sure you get some invincibility there, too.

00:16:54.820 --> 00:17:05.980
But I will say that I think if the level is going to be this small, because we're used to these shmups that just, they're endlessly scrolling.

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:10.100
And you don't, you never know when it's going to end.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:21.540
And it all starts to blur together that, like, it's this small of a game, of a game space that, like, it's got to have some extra challenge to it.

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:30.380
And I think that, like, the challenge that's added to the level itself is kind of countered by the fact that you have some defensive measures.

00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:41.600
Like, you can dodge things if you're, like, if you're moving slow enough already, then you can kind of use that turnaround animation in your favor.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:43.420
But I don't know.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:46.820
I think there's a balance there that it's sort of hitting.

00:17:47.260 --> 00:17:54.920
Yeah, I'll also admit that I, that the thing you mentioned about kind of the barrel roll you can do, I almost didn't utilize that at all.

00:17:55.060 --> 00:17:55.960
And I probably should have.

00:17:56.240 --> 00:17:58.760
I only utilized it when I was trying to land.

00:17:58.960 --> 00:17:59.840
So I know what you mean.

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:00.640
Oh, gotcha. Yeah.

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:10.440
But yeah, I was just feeling like, enemies, since they spawn kind of at random, it was just like, as soon as I turn around and my backs turn, enemies just spawn immediately behind me and shoot me.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:14.520
Where it's like, well, like, if I knew they were there, I wouldn't have turned around, but they weren't there.

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:18.240
They appeared there as soon as I turned around, and that bothered me.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:32.780
And one thing that I want to point out, just going back to the movie for a second here, it's funny that this game has such a, you know, for a shmup, non-standard structure.

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:45.700
Because the plot of this movie, and there are lines and dialogue conversations in this movie that literally codify a shmup.

00:18:46.340 --> 00:18:59.780
Like, they actually talk about, like, we've always sort of called out, like, why the hell are they just sending this one guy to take off, to take out this entire air force or this entire armada?

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:02.700
Like, can't they send him some more resources?

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:06.960
And then, in the plot of this movie, they actually do that.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:12.560
And then when they make a game out of the movie about games, they make it not that.

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:18.000
Sorry. I just think that that's super weird, and so many missed opportunities here.

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:24.760
Well, just remember, because that's because they made a game that wasn't about a movie, and then somebody said, I'll pay you money to just port this.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:30.140
They could have licensed any game to rename.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:31.480
Yes, I totally agree.

00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.920
Why couldn't Image Fight be the last Starfighter?

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:35.500
That's true. I hear you loud and clear.

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:40.660
And I'm only picking on Image Fight because we just recorded that episode two weeks ago, so no biggie there.

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:43.040
Just one other thing.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:49.580
The game really wants you to believe that the ability to control your speed is important.

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:57.580
It is something that you do have power over by choosing how fast you want to go.

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:06.000
And I guess it matters most in the small detail that we haven't talked about yet for the base that there are things on the base.

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:14.780
And it is a little unclear what those things are, but there are things on the base that you can fly over, and then there are others that you can't fly over and you will crash into.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:24.180
And I don't know if anybody else was able to figure out the secret sauce that was like, oh, when the graphic looks like this, you'll crash into it.

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:28.000
But I certainly couldn't, and it led to a lot of surprise deaths.

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:30.500
Yeah. So I guess I should have been playing slower?

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:46.420
Okay, so the whole speed thing, basically you should be playing as close to standard shmup scrolling speed as you can until there's like a thing that kind of looks like a pickup.

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:52.340
So you might fly into it thinking you'll get a power up, but then you just explode.

00:20:54.380 --> 00:21:00.180
Otherwise, if you go any faster, you will just run into the things that Mike was talking about.

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:08.000
The only thing I could tell is that these things that you can hit and blow up, like they have like a drop shadow.

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:13.980
That's the only way that I could tell, but that is not legible at the speed you're usually going at.

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:50.620
To move on to the landing sequence, something you guys were trying to jump the gun on and I had to reel you back in for a second.

00:21:51.360 --> 00:22:03.420
Landing is something that the manual tries to describe and then you realize, and I think Joe was coming to the same conclusion, Sean having not read the manual wouldn't know this, that it doesn't actually tell you.

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:06.180
I read that part of the manual after the fact.

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:07.720
Okay, got it, got it.

00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:17.220
That's like ASMR right there. It doesn't actually tell you how to land, it just mentions landing.

00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:19.880
It says like hold back.

00:22:20.300 --> 00:22:26.640
Right, right. And it's like, okay, but I could really use like an input now if I was a manual, right?

00:22:26.660 --> 00:22:28.200
I'd be talking about the controls.

00:22:28.500 --> 00:22:33.880
And so to land, for those of you who maybe played this game and still haven't figured it out,

00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:42.800
you have to approach the landing strip at the end of each level so that when you are scrolling from left to right,

00:22:43.120 --> 00:22:45.800
it doesn't work if you go right to left, believe it or not.

00:22:45.940 --> 00:22:51.920
If you turn your ship around, you have to go back to before the landing strip and then turn it around again.

00:22:52.460 --> 00:22:58.320
Because whether or not you're blowing this place up, you still have to follow the air traffic control laws.

00:22:58.320 --> 00:22:59.560
Yeah, absolutely.

00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:02.280
Otherwise, they just won't let you land, right?

00:23:02.440 --> 00:23:04.100
No, who knows what the explanation is.

00:23:04.120 --> 00:23:06.980
You're cleared to land if you're coming in this way, even if you're blowing us up.

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:14.880
Right. So basically, you have to be at the slowest speed as you're approaching this landing strip.

00:23:15.200 --> 00:23:22.680
And then, and only then, if you're on the slowest speed, do you, as you're hovering over the landing strip,

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:25.640
you press to slow down one last time.

00:23:25.640 --> 00:23:28.820
And that is what causes it to land.

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:39.560
You cannot be at a faster speed than slow, than slowest, and just, and just keep spamming the left button enough,

00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:42.320
or, yeah, it would be the left button because you're facing the left side.

00:23:42.660 --> 00:23:48.900
But did you ever try that and feel like, because I, I, I never was maybe specifically trying to be at the slowest,

00:23:48.960 --> 00:23:50.180
like, thinking, like, this is what I have to do.

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:54.180
But I was at the slowest speed, I thought, for a lot of the time because I was just trying to figure it out.

00:23:54.340 --> 00:23:57.700
And then I would hit the, like, slow down button and it would just turn me around.

00:23:58.220 --> 00:24:01.780
And, no, it works every time, in my opinion, once you know that.

00:24:01.780 --> 00:24:04.340
And I only know that because of game FAQs.

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:05.460
I had to read it.

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:07.020
I literally couldn't wrap my head around it.

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:09.260
At least 60% of the time it works all the time.

00:24:09.400 --> 00:24:13.020
Is there, is there, like a, I mean, how lined up with the runway?

00:24:13.200 --> 00:24:16.040
Does your shadow have to be lined up or does your ship have to be lined up?

00:24:16.100 --> 00:24:17.460
Your ship has to be lined up.

00:24:17.780 --> 00:24:19.580
The shadow? Yeah, it's the ship.

00:24:19.760 --> 00:24:21.060
The ship. It is the ship.

00:24:21.220 --> 00:24:23.760
Okay. Because, you know, intuitively I would think the shadow.

00:24:24.080 --> 00:24:26.580
But then, but I tried both, too.

00:24:26.580 --> 00:24:28.480
And it happened sometimes and other times it didn't.

00:24:28.560 --> 00:24:30.460
And I could just never, I could just never nail it down.

00:24:32.360 --> 00:24:33.240
Yeah, it was tough.

00:24:33.420 --> 00:24:35.680
It was, it was real tough, guys.

00:24:36.040 --> 00:24:42.340
No, I do agree that it's, it's one of those things that's almost impossible until you find out the secret sauce.

00:24:42.340 --> 00:24:47.200
Like, there, there was a moment for me where I was actually just thinking, like, I'm not going to be able to play this game.

00:24:47.500 --> 00:24:48.740
Like, it's not going to work.

00:24:48.860 --> 00:24:54.680
So I went to game FAQs, read that, and just immediately landed every single time afterwards.

00:24:54.680 --> 00:24:58.200
Not bragging again, but it, that's how it went.

00:24:58.620 --> 00:25:03.820
And, and, and the funny thing is, is that I proceeded to read the rest of the game FAQ.

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:07.800
The only FAQ written about this game on the NES.

00:25:08.520 --> 00:25:12.760
And the rest of the FAQ just trashes the game so hard.

00:25:12.960 --> 00:25:20.180
Like, unnecessarily, just like, can't believe that this person who wrote this simultaneously wrote this wall of text.

00:25:20.180 --> 00:25:23.180
And continues to berate the game the entire time.

00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:30.480
Yeah, I, for some reason, did not have the mental clarity to go to game FAQs.

00:25:30.580 --> 00:25:35.920
I just thought, like, in this day and age, where every game has something written about it.

00:25:35.980 --> 00:25:40.360
I just googled, like, how do you land in the last Starfighter NES?

00:25:41.060 --> 00:25:45.040
And was surprised to find nothing really there.

00:25:45.640 --> 00:25:46.680
Yeah. So.

00:25:47.060 --> 00:25:50.120
There's nothing about anything about the last Starfighter on the NES.

00:25:50.180 --> 00:25:56.040
I am surprised about, and we've seen this a lot recently, where, like, are these games rare?

00:25:56.260 --> 00:25:57.260
Are they worth anything?

00:25:57.560 --> 00:26:01.520
Like, did people just not play a lot of NES games in the 1990s?

00:26:01.860 --> 00:26:05.240
It's surprising how little information I'm able to find about some of these games.

00:26:05.440 --> 00:26:09.840
We've, you know, we've heard of the movie, or at least watched the clips on YouTube.

00:26:10.220 --> 00:26:13.660
And now it's like, but nobody's talking about the NES game?

00:26:13.800 --> 00:26:16.400
That's weird. I sense a conspiracy.

00:26:17.800 --> 00:26:19.140
It's a cover-up.

00:26:19.960 --> 00:26:27.500
Once you land the ship on the base, though, you're taken to a bonus game, or call it a game, if you will.

00:26:27.580 --> 00:26:32.560
It's a bonus screen that the manual refers to as the fuel rod chamber.

00:26:32.560 --> 00:26:37.520
So I guess you're doing something in there to get enough fuel to go on to the next base.

00:26:37.520 --> 00:26:44.180
But all it really is is just two squares flashing, one after the other.

00:26:44.540 --> 00:26:46.180
One has the word quit on it.

00:26:46.280 --> 00:26:47.520
The other has a number.

00:26:47.720 --> 00:26:50.800
That number is going to be the amount of points that the game gives you.

00:26:50.800 --> 00:27:01.220
And you have to press the A button while hopefully the number is flashing, or else you press the quit button, and that just means the bonus level's over.

00:27:01.720 --> 00:27:08.280
And if you get the number, then it moves you on to the next stage in the pyramid of the fuel rod chamber.

00:27:08.440 --> 00:27:09.660
The only guy knows that it's dumb.

00:27:09.660 --> 00:27:11.720
Thank you, please. You don't need to do it.

00:27:11.720 --> 00:27:13.280
So thankful you saved me.

00:27:13.480 --> 00:27:23.840
Yeah. This is the worst excuse for an interactive minigame that I think that we've seen on this console.

00:27:24.480 --> 00:27:31.500
It's literally just like, try to match the clock speed of this, and that's it.

00:27:31.940 --> 00:27:33.420
It takes no...

00:27:33.420 --> 00:27:34.600
It takes...

00:27:35.240 --> 00:27:36.620
I'm done talking about it.

00:27:36.620 --> 00:27:41.180
Yeah, by the time you get to the highest up one, I mean, the highest one, it's got to be pure luck.

00:27:41.180 --> 00:27:46.380
I just don't believe someone could be fast enough to actually get that on skill.

00:27:46.960 --> 00:27:54.980
No. There's only 15 levels, but they do get a lot more challenging as it goes on, especially with the way that the enemy ships behave.

00:27:54.980 --> 00:27:56.700
You will die a lot.

00:27:56.700 --> 00:27:58.740
You will run into things on the base a lot.

00:27:58.740 --> 00:28:05.160
You will just succumb to the surprise attacks that Joe was referring to, where it's like,

00:28:05.160 --> 00:28:11.220
well, it's one thing to be able to deal with the ships as they're on screen, but it's another thing when they just appear suddenly,

00:28:11.220 --> 00:28:14.440
and you just can't move fast enough to get away from them.

00:28:14.660 --> 00:28:19.660
Yeah. But with only 15 levels, right, like, is it...

00:28:19.660 --> 00:28:21.660
And you can leave whenever, right?

00:28:21.740 --> 00:28:24.360
Like, there's no consequence for leaving early.

00:28:24.360 --> 00:28:31.980
So assuming that you just get to, successfully get to the end of each stage and know to slow down and know how to land,

00:28:32.360 --> 00:28:39.960
you could theoretically play this game very fast and beat it very fast if you knew where the ships were spawning out of.

00:28:40.460 --> 00:28:42.960
Is it like, shouldn't it just been an infinite loop?

00:28:43.120 --> 00:28:44.240
Why only 15 levels?

00:28:44.240 --> 00:28:46.100
Well, hold on.

00:28:46.600 --> 00:28:54.520
I've found that we aren't very keen on a game stretching itself out just by repeating itself.

00:28:54.800 --> 00:29:01.100
So I almost, like, thank it for its mercy that it's not doing that.

00:29:01.100 --> 00:29:04.160
I'm glad I spent $60 for 20 minutes of gameplay.

00:29:05.520 --> 00:29:11.540
When you said you can just leave at any time, I actually thought you meant that, like, you can just get up, put the controller down,

00:29:11.640 --> 00:29:13.180
and walk away from this game at any time.

00:29:13.180 --> 00:29:15.060
Just leave. Because that's your first thought.

00:29:15.200 --> 00:29:17.220
You see what I'm saying? That's your first thought.

00:29:18.500 --> 00:29:25.940
But you also, not to subvert the question you asked, but I kind of agree with Sean.

00:29:25.940 --> 00:29:28.460
I just think, like, make more game if you're going to make more game.

00:29:28.740 --> 00:29:30.360
Otherwise, like, I'll be done.

00:29:30.360 --> 00:29:36.500
But you also mentioned that you will crash into the ship or to, like, parts of the ship often.

00:29:36.700 --> 00:29:42.420
Did anyone else feel like that was a lot of those things are, like, hard to tell what's 3D and what's not?

00:29:42.440 --> 00:29:44.680
Oh, yeah. I crashed into a lot of things I thought were part of the background.

00:29:44.880 --> 00:29:47.800
There's definitely, like, I was describing it earlier.

00:29:47.920 --> 00:29:55.880
There's, like, a drop shadow that'll show you what is crash-into-able and what isn't.

00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:58.820
But it definitely blends into the stage.

00:29:58.940 --> 00:30:07.320
Right. So, it's not, like, if they had just given it a contrast in color, then, holy shit, you solved cancer.

00:30:07.560 --> 00:30:08.960
Like, that's all you gotta do.

00:30:09.240 --> 00:30:10.800
But they didn't do that.

00:30:11.280 --> 00:30:13.720
So, you have to kind of fly slow.

00:30:15.220 --> 00:30:16.960
And it's silly.

00:30:17.220 --> 00:30:22.280
At the end of the game, as you scroll, well, before I get to the end of the game, actually,

00:30:22.300 --> 00:30:24.400
there's a different scrolling thing I wanted to talk about.

00:30:24.400 --> 00:30:28.420
And that is those base destruction sequences.

00:30:28.980 --> 00:30:41.840
After the fuel rod chamber bonus game, and after you land, you see the annihilation of the alien ship level that you were just on.

00:30:43.060 --> 00:30:45.620
But it's kind of autopilot.

00:30:45.860 --> 00:30:52.340
Like, you can steer the ship from left to right, but you can't die in the explosion, right?

00:30:52.340 --> 00:30:54.060
Like, you just watch it blow up.

00:30:54.140 --> 00:30:55.320
It's there to be cool.

00:30:55.320 --> 00:31:00.220
But, like, why is it on autopilot if you can control the ship, right?

00:31:00.340 --> 00:31:04.300
Like, and you're just watching the whole level blow up again.

00:31:04.480 --> 00:31:07.860
It's like, shouldn't there be one last, like, challenge here?

00:31:07.860 --> 00:31:12.580
I don't know if I would have liked that in the actual game, but, like, thinking about substance.

00:31:12.580 --> 00:31:22.220
Like, isn't this just weird that, like, at the end of every level, you just kind of watch the same cutscene over and over again where the level destroys itself?

00:31:23.320 --> 00:31:27.060
I thought it was, I thought it was, I was thinking of it the opposite way.

00:31:27.180 --> 00:31:35.980
I was like, oh, okay, there's this cutscene, and as an added perk, they let you have, maintain control of the ship during the cutscene.

00:31:36.400 --> 00:31:40.420
Rather than, like, this is a level, but nothing can happen to you.

00:31:40.500 --> 00:31:42.180
So I guess it just depends on the way you look at it.

00:31:42.580 --> 00:31:51.060
Yeah, had the levels not started with you needing to get into, like, the safety corral zone to be able to control the ship, you know what I'm talking about?

00:31:51.060 --> 00:31:54.860
There's, like, those five beach balls that, like, yeah.

00:31:55.440 --> 00:31:57.480
Right, once you enter that, you have control of your ship.

00:31:57.540 --> 00:32:04.480
But had that not been there, I would have thought that they just didn't know how to program a cutscene and that you could just control the ship at all times.

00:32:04.600 --> 00:32:07.960
That was an immediate introduction to frustration.

00:32:07.960 --> 00:32:16.380
I don't know what it is, but that, not having control of the ship for those first few seconds, like, immediately made me kind of upset.

00:32:17.040 --> 00:32:32.640
And I don't know if that's just, like, my reptile brain that's been getting worse and worse and just getting rotted by video games, but that just didn't feel right.

00:32:32.820 --> 00:32:33.940
Did it felt right to you guys?

00:32:34.260 --> 00:32:44.600
No. Well, I don't think I had the same frustration, but I was, like, checking my controller, making sure I was, like, plugged in, and, like, you know, I was a little concerned for a moment.

00:32:44.600 --> 00:32:53.660
I don't think this is related to the movie, but after you've finished the final level, you scroll past a bunch of text that says,

00:32:54.100 --> 00:32:57.020
Good Zappin', dot, dot, dot, turkey.

00:32:57.820 --> 00:32:59.920
Yes. What the heck is that?

00:33:01.840 --> 00:33:05.520
Sean, do they ever say Good Zappin' Turkey in the movie?

00:33:05.520 --> 00:33:23.520
As the definitive Last Starfighter fan here, I'm almost positive they didn't say Turkey once, and I did watch the scene where, you know, his alien friends meet his human friends, and, like, they say,

00:33:23.660 --> 00:33:26.340
How do you do? And I do well.

00:33:26.340 --> 00:33:27.140
How do you do?

00:33:27.360 --> 00:33:29.220
And not once did they say Turkey.

00:33:29.220 --> 00:33:40.700
It's just interesting, because I also believe it's in the original Iridium game as well, so almost confirms that it wouldn't be from the movie, but why not just change it to be in the movie?

00:33:40.900 --> 00:33:48.740
And while we're talking about things that you could change to be in the movie, Sean, as the biggest Last Starfighter fan in the room, were you surprised that there—

00:33:48.740 --> 00:33:50.200
Yeah, in the world, I should say.

00:33:50.200 --> 00:33:59.660
Were you surprised that there was no, like, after you kill a certain amount of enemies, press A and B at the same time to launch the Death Blossom?

00:34:00.840 --> 00:34:11.900
Yes. I was gonna mention the Death Blossom, because that was one of the scenes on movie clips on YouTube.

00:34:11.900 --> 00:34:18.760
Uh, but the thing is that I only watched all the movie clips on YouTube after I played the game.

00:34:19.240 --> 00:34:29.480
Uh, like, several hours, like, maybe 24 hours between playing the game and watching the definitive movie clips, this makes you a fan, videos.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:33.680
Uh, so I only learned about the Death Blossom after the fact.

00:34:33.820 --> 00:34:38.540
But if you're asking me after the fact, yeah, I think it's a missed opportunity.

00:34:38.540 --> 00:34:44.700
That's, like, the biggest scene in the movie, if movie clips is to be believed.

00:34:45.800 --> 00:35:02.000
Well, it's definitely the coolest, because, you know, there's a lot of talk about the Death Blossom, and then to actually see it, uh, you know, again, I'm not saying that the graphics look, uh, great compared to the Marvel Cinematic Universe movies, but it sold me.

00:35:02.000 --> 00:35:03.920
I was like, hey, that looks great, you know?

00:35:04.040 --> 00:35:05.380
Like, I'm buying it.

00:35:05.480 --> 00:35:06.560
He's doing all that.

00:35:06.560 --> 00:35:13.960
And maybe it's because they leaned into the video game feel of it all, especially the, you know, 80s arcade aesthetic of it.

00:35:14.160 --> 00:35:23.120
